  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through next Friday)\nIssued at 1230 PM CDT Fri Oct 9 2026\n\nLong term forecast has not changed much, with more certainty in\nthe forecast through the middle of next week and less for late in\nthe week into the weekend. Upper level ridge builds across the\nPlains with the upper low on the West Coast and the hurricane off\nto the east. This ridge will help temperatures climb to well above\nnormal readings (10-15 degrees above normal) for the start to\nmiddle of next week.\n\nStill some model differences in just how the West Coast trough\nmoves east, with fairly significant model differences between\nmodels and between ensemble members of the same model. This leads\nto a more uncertain forecast, especially with regards to POPs and\nrain totals. With that in mind, not going to deviate much from the\nNBM and the model blends. \n\nThere is a more consistent pattern in showing a stronger front \nand cooler air mass moving into the region by late in the week and\ninto the weekend. Blends are showing highs only in the 70s by \nnext Friday and Saturday, and this may be too warm if the higher \nPOPs pan out and keep more post-frontal precipitation and cloud \ncover in place.",
